# Hackedbox Change Log

## Hackedbox 0.9.x

### 2026-09-28

* Moved HbTK out of the Hackedbox window manager source tree to continue development as an independent toolkit.
* Updated Hackedbox documentation to reflect the separation of HbTK from the window manager.
* Added documentation for `hbsetbg`, including usage, options, background configuration, positioning, and background rotation.
* Changed `root.background.timer` to use minutes.
* Continued cleanup and modernization of the source tree and documentation.

### 2026-09-27

* Continued development of Runbox and keyboard input handling.
* Continued development and integration of KeyManager.
* Continued restructuring Hackedbox around dedicated managers and components.
* Continued development of the StyleEngine and classic window/frame styling.
* Continued development of multi-screen background handling.

### 2026-09-26

* Added the initial StyleEngine as a separate component of the Hackedbox style system.
* Moved style processing out of `Screen.cpp` into StyleEngine.
* Began restructuring Hackedbox around dedicated managers rather than keeping functionality inside Screen.
* Added MenuManager to replace the older RootMenu/BaseMenu responsibilities.
* Added KeyManager for keyboard shortcut and key binding management.
* Added Runbox for the Hackedbox run dialog.
* Added `hbsudo` for privileged Hackedbox operations.
* Added dialog styling support for `hbsudo`.
* Continued modernization of the menu and configuration systems.

#### HbTK

* Began development of HbTK as a reusable native C++ GUI toolkit.
* Added the initial application, window, widget, event, drawing, dialog, and container components.
* Added Style and StyleEngine components.
* Added support for building HbTK as a library.
* Installed HbTK headers under `/usr/include/hbtk/`.
* Installed the HbTK static library as `/usr/lib/libhbtk.a`.
* Added an initial HbTK test window.
* Began moving Hackedbox-style window and frame rendering concepts into HbTK.
* Established HbTK as a reusable toolkit rather than a collection of application-specific widgets.

### 2026-09-25

* Continued development of `hbsetbg` background handling.
* Improved background handling for multi-screen X displays.
* Began automatic detection and handling of multiple monitors and combined desktop backgrounds.
* Continued modernization of the Hackedbox background system.

### 2026-09-24

* Continued development of the Hackedbox style system and resource handling.
* Expanded style support for window and menu appearance.
* Added support for newer menu, window, alpha, and dialog resources.
* Added `window.dialog.*` resources for Hackedbox dialog styling.
* Continued correction of style resource loading and fallback behavior.
* Updated styles while retaining their existing fonts, colors, gradients, and layout.

### 2026-09-23

* Began updating the existing Hackedbox styles for the 0.9.x style system.
* Began the transition from the legacy style implementation toward the new StyleEngine architecture.

## Hackedbox 0.8.8

### 2026-09-20

* Added solid color background support to `hbsetbg` with `-color`/`--color`.
* Added Imlib2 dependency detection to the build configuration.
* Renamed the default style file to lowercase `default` to avoid case-related menu naming issues.
* Removed the obsolete `steelblue` style from the styles build list.

## Hackedbox 0.8.7

The 0.8.7 development cycle completed the major conversion and modernization of the original Blackbox-derived codebase.

### Core

* Completed the conversion from legacy Blackbox naming to Hackedbox naming throughout the source.

* Completed conversion of legacy `.hh` headers to `.hpp`.

* Completed conversion of legacy `.cc` sources to `.cpp`.

* Updated copyright headers to:

  Copyright (c) 2026 Kevin Day <blame582@gmail.com>

* Removed obsolete build artifacts and legacy source files.

* Established Hackedbox-specific configuration and behavior rather than maintaining Blackbox compatibility.

* Marked old Blackbox and Fluxbox styles as incompatible with the current style implementation.

### Style System

* Replaced the original style handling with the new Hackedbox style system.
* Began development of StyleEngine as the foundation for future style compatibility and resource handling.
* Expanded style parsing and resource handling.
* Added the new `.style` configuration format.
* Added `root.background` support to style files.
* Moved background handling to `hbsetbg`.
* Expanded style resources for menu frames, titles, text, textures, fonts, colors, and gradients.
* Updated the Default style.
* Fixed style fallback problems caused by resources not being read correctly from the new format.
* Continued development of menu and window styling resources.

### Backgrounds

* Established `hbsetbg` as the Hackedbox background-setting utility.
* Added support for image backgrounds through `root.background`.
* Replaced the old `hbsetroot` image-setting path because it did not provide the required image functionality.
* Integrated `hbsetbg` with the Hackedbox style system.

### Runbox

* Began replacing the old `hbrun` implementation.
* Reworked the launcher GUI and its integration with Hackedbox styling.
* Fixed the launcher from displaying a broken or white window to displaying a functional empty launcher box.
* Continued work on launcher focus, cursor, styling, and rendering.

### Menu System

* Began the new MenuManager implementation.
* Reworked menu initialization and menu-file handling.
* Continued migration of menu classes and resources to Hackedbox naming and APIs.
* Added root-menu list management.
* Added and refined menu resources for:

  * title fonts
  * frame textures
  * frame colors
  * text colors
  * highlighted menu items
  * justification
  * bullets
* Continued debugging menu rendering and style resource loading.

### Screen and Resources

* Modernized `Screen.hpp` and `Screen.cpp`.
* Updated HbScreen resource structures.
* Added and refined handling for:

  * window styles
  * menu styles
  * focus behavior
  * auto raise
  * click raise
  * workspace configuration
  * placement policy
  * edge snapping thresholds
  * row and column placement direction
  * background configuration
* Removed obsolete commented clock/date resource handling.
* Corrected header declarations to match the current Screen implementation.

### Configuration

* Continued migration away from the original Blackbox configuration model.
* Established Hackedbox-specific resources and behavior.
* Updated Greenday to use the current Hackedbox style and background system.

### HbTK

* Continued development of HbTK as the toolkit for Hackedbox applications.
* Developed native X/XLibre-based widgets without GTK, Qt, or FLTK.
* Continued development of:

  * Widget
  * MainWindow
  * Splitter
  * Painter
  * terminal widgets
* Cleaned up internal class naming so toolkit components do not unnecessarily use an `Hb` prefix.

### Terminally-Hacked

* Continued development of the native XLibre/X11 terminal.
* Added Xft and Fontconfig-based font handling.
* Resolved Fontconfig/Xft linking issues.
* Continued development without Qt, GTK, or FLTK dependencies.

## Planned Development

The following work was not considered complete during the 0.8.x development cycle:

* Integrated Hackedbox hotkey system.
* Regional window snapping.
* 1/4 and 1/2 screen window placement.
* Optional tiling-style placement.
* Integrated tray support inside the Hackedbox menu.
* Menu icon support.
* File manager.
* Hackedpad editor.
* Completion of Terminally-Hacked.
* Replacement of remaining external desktop applications.
* Further architectural redesign of Hackedbox.

## Compatibility

Hackedbox is now a substantially diverged descendant of the original Blackbox
codebase.

The following are not maintained as compatibility targets:

* Blackbox styles.
* Fluxbox styles.
* Legacy Hackedbox styles that are incompatible with the current style system.

Hackedbox is developed around its own configuration, style, toolkit, and
desktop-component architecture.

## Historical Development

### 2026-08-23 — Hackedbox 0.8.6

#### Core

* Began the major source and toolkit modernization following the 0.8.5 release.
* Converted remaining Blackbox and `B`-prefixed source to Hackedbox and `Hb` naming.
* Renamed `.hh` and `.cc` files to `.hpp` and `.cpp`.
* Updated include paths and copyright headers.
* Removed obsolete Blackbox and `bbkeys` components.

#### HbTK

* Began the HbTK toolkit.
* Added Application, Window, Widget, Dialog, Entry, Button, Frame, TitleBar,
  Splitter, Painter, Style, StyleEngine, Event, and related components.
* Added `libhbtk.a` to the build.
* Began integrating HbTK with Hackedbox.

#### Runbox

* Added the initial HbTK-based Runbox.
* Began integrating Runbox with the root menu.

#### Styles

* Updated style handling.
* Introduced `root.background` for desktop background images.

#### hbsetbg

* Added the Hackedbox `hbsetbg` image-setting utility.
* Added center, tile, stretch-to-center, and stretch-to-edge modes.
* Replaced the old `hsetbg` usage.
* Removed obsolete `hbsetroot` background handling.

#### Build System

* Updated Automake and Autoconf configuration for HbTK and static-library
  building.
* Added RANLIB support.
* Added subdir-objects handling.

#### Documentation

* Added initial `hbsetbg` documentation.
* Updated manual generation.

#### Menu

* Updated menu execution handling.
* Began integration of the internal HbTK Runbox.

#### Status

* Hackedbox, HbTK, and `hbsetbg` built successfully.
* Internal Runbox integration was not yet functional at runtime.
